{
  "description": "This is a protocol to dilute and spot bacteria for isolation and quantification. Bacterial samples are passed through 10, 10x serial dilutions with each dilution spotted onto agar. This can process up to 40 samples at a time (5 plates x 8 wells (1 column) per plate). \nPlates should be preloaded with the bacterial samples in column 1 and 90 µL of dilution buffer or media in columns 2-12. Agar plates should be prepared by filling Nunc Omnitrays with 30 mL of melted agar. These should be dried on as flat a surface as possible to ensure consistent heights across the plate.\nCalibration on the agar plate should be performed so that the tips are just barely touching the agar as the \"top of the well\".",
  "tags": [
    "33y0f3.ot2.apiv2.py",
    "Microbiology"
  ],
